"text": " It was the last game of his career, a World Cup final. And Zinedine Zidane walked off with a red card. July 9th, 2006. Berlin, France against Italy. Seven minutes in, Zidane takes a penalty and chips it. It hits the crossbar, bounces down over the line. Twelve minutes later, Marco Martirazzi heads Italy level. 1-1. Extra time. Zidane and Martirazzi exchange words. Zidane walks away, then turns around and headbutts him in the chest The referee didn't see it, the fourth official did Red card, Zidane walks past the World Cup trophy and off the pitch, forever Italy won on penalties And Zidane was still voted the best player of the tournament Matarazzi later said he insulted Zidane's sister Zidane never repeated the words Would you have sent him off? Tell me in the comments",
